From 93b9f4b40327160baee5d23b9bd59528429a2ef7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Stosse <florian.stosse@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:27:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [e-acsl] memcmp replacement: do not reject overlapping
 arguments

With `-e-acsl-replace-libc-functions` (`e-acsl-gcc --libc-replacements`),
`eacsl_builtin_memcmp` called `validate_overlapping_spaces` on its two
arguments, with the name "memcpy". Any `memcmp(s1, s2, n)` with `n > 0` and
overlapping ranges, including `memcmp(p, p, n)`, aborted the program with
"memcpy: overlapping memory areas".

The call was copied from `eacsl_builtin_memcpy`. `memcmp` only reads its
arguments and has no `restrict` parameter (C17 7.24.4.1), so overlapping or
identical ranges are valid, as they already are for the `strcmp` and
`strncmp` replacements, which check only that both arguments are allocated.

Remove the overlap check. The checks that both ranges are allocated stay.
The new test `builtin/memcmp.c` (the suite of the libc replacements, which
had no `memcmp` test) compares identical, overlapping and disjoint ranges of
one array.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../e-acsl/libc_replacements/e_acsl_string.c  |  1 -
 plugins/e-acsl/tests/builtin/memcmp.c         | 12 +++
 .../tests/builtin/oracle/gen_memcmp.0.c       | 93 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../tests/builtin/oracle/memcmp.0.res.oracle  | 18 ++++
 4 files changed, 123 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 plugins/e-acsl/tests/builtin/memcmp.c
 create mode 100644 plugins/e-acsl/tests/builtin/oracle/gen_memcmp.0.c
 create mode 100644 plugins/e-acsl/tests/builtin/oracle/memcmp.0.res.oracle

diff --git a/plugins/e-acsl/share/e-acsl/libc_replacements/e_acsl_string.c b/plugins/e-acsl/share/e-acsl/libc_replacements/e_acsl_string.c
index 18de67a564..c9369eb556 100644
--- a/plugins/e-acsl/share/e-acsl/libc_replacements/e_acsl_string.c
+++ b/plugins/e-acsl/share/e-acsl/libc_replacements/e_acsl_string.c
@@ -237,7 +237,6 @@ void *eacsl_builtin_memset(void *s, int c, size_t n) {
 int eacsl_builtin_memcmp(const void *s1, const void *s2, size_t n) {
   validate_allocated_space((void *)s1, n, "memcmp", "space 1 ");
   validate_allocated_space((void *)s2, n, "memcmp", "space 2 ");
-  validate_overlapping_spaces((uintptr_t)s1, n, (uintptr_t)s2, n, "memcpy");
   return memcmp(s1, s2, n);
 }
 
diff --git a/plugins/e-acsl/tests/builtin/memcmp.c b/plugins/e-acsl/tests/builtin/memcmp.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..1748beacae
--- /dev/null
+++ b/plugins/e-acsl/tests/builtin/memcmp.c
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+#include <string.h>
+
+int main() {
+  char buf[8] = "abababa";
+  // memcmp only reads its arguments: identical or overlapping ranges are valid
+  int same = memcmp(buf, buf, 4);
+  int overlap = memcmp(buf, buf + 2, 4);
+  int disjoint = memcmp(buf, buf + 4, 3);
+  //@ assert same == 0;
+  //@ assert overlap == 0;
+  //@ assert disjoint == 0;
+}
